  "chapter_note": "Heavy damage (88.7%). Chapter has a clear three-part structure: (1) extended narrative frame about an ugly elect at a gathering being laughed at — segments 4-55 are dominated by hagiographic-pastoral material, (2) a substantive cosmological teaching about pearl-formation (segments 65-128) which IS substrate — describing the natural process of how rain drops fall into the sea, mingle with sweet waters, and are molded into pearls in oysters, with divers retrieving them. This is correspondential natural-process teaching where both sides stay within the cosmic-natural system. (3) explicit ecclesial application (129-142) mapping pearls→souls, oysters→flesh, divers→apostles, kings→Aeons of Greatness, and finally hortatory exhortation 'become beautiful pearls' (143-149). The seam at segment 129 ('This also is the manner in which the holy Church is likened to it') is textbook allegorical pivot — and the score data flagged it. The pearl-formation cosmology (66-128) is the substrate core: a Persian-style natural-science correspondence about how precious substances form. The pastoral narrative frame and ecclesial application are clearly later editorial layers.",
